    "n_2b2e0e3fe96a1686": {
      "id": "n_2b2e0e3fe96a1686",
      "title": "Files live where they live",
      "summary": "One reference, several locations.",
      "content": [
        {
          "id": "b_8f19e046d92927fc",
          "type": "markdown",
          "value": "A file reference holds every place that file exists. A location recorded\nrelative to a **named root** resolves on every machine that has mapped that\nroot; an absolute one only works where it was recorded.\n\nThe dot says which: green is here, red is missing, hollow means this machine\nhas never been told where that root is.\n\nIn a browser tab paths are recorded but inert. The desktop build opens them.",
          "label": "",
          "meta": {}
        }
      ],
      "tags": [
        "reference"
      ],
      "status": null,
      "x": 560,
      "y": 40,
      "fields": {},
      "color": null,
      "created": "2026-09-16T02:15:00.122Z",
      "updated": "2026-09-16T02:15:00.122Z"
    },
    "n_b4236e75982a5808": {
      "id": "n_b4236e75982a5808",
      "title": "It is a graph, not a tree",
      "summary": "Draw a second line whenever something gains a new meaning.",
      "content": [
        {
          "id": "b_c64b1e870ad737e5",
          "type": "markdown",
          "value": "Nothing has to move to gain a new association. Add the edge and keep both.",
          "label": "",
          "meta": {}
        }
      ],
